.claude/worktrees
.rubymate/
.bundle/
coverage/
pkg/
vendor/bundle/
.rspec_status
**/.DS_Store
# YARD build artifacts. spec/yard_documentation_spec.rb shells out to
# `yard stats`, which writes both on every full suite run.
.yardoc/
doc/
*.gem

# Real taxpayer return information. NEVER commit — §7216, and Document 1 §C
# requires the reference corpus to be fully synthetic. Use these locally to
# verify the engine; never lift figures from them into a fixture or corpus case.
docs/us-taxes/returns/
*-1040*.pdf
*-1120*.pdf
*-1065*.pdf
.env

# Generated by the consuming application at vendor time, into its own copy under
# rails/vendor/tax-engine — the upstream revision plus a digest over the vendored
# files. It describes a vendored tree, never this one, so it must never be
# committed here. tax_engine.gemspec excludes it from spec.files as well.
lib/tax_engine/vendored_revision.rb

# Anonymised third-party returns used to verify the engine locally. Removing
# direct identifiers makes a return pseudonymous, not anonymous: the figures are
# still someone's tax return information. Keep them out of git and out of the
# corpus — see 016's spec, which decided exactly this point.
spec/fixtures/returns/*-tax-return-*.txt
